  "Soper GA (1939), 'The curious career of Typhoid Mary', Bulletin of the New York Academy of Medicine 15(10):698-712: the 1906 Oyster Bay outbreak; Soper traced it to the cook, Mary Mallon, and suspected ice cream with raw peaches",
  "Mary Mallon was the first person in the United States identified as a healthy (asymptomatic) carrier of Salmonella Typhi; doctors suspected her gallbladder",
